.TH FSTAB-MANAGER 1 "2026" "fstab Manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fstab\-manager \- desktop app for managing fstab mounts, backups and home links
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fstab\-manager
.RB [ \-\-size " \fIWIDTHxHEIGHT\fR]"
.RB [ \-\-no\-notify ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the fstab Manager window. It shows fstab mounts with live status, explains problems and
offers one\-click fixes, mounts drives without a reboot, previews every change as a diff before
writing, manages home\-folder symlinks, and notices when a disk is plugged in.
.PP
The window is a native application using the system's WebKitGTK; there is no browser and no
network port. Writing /etc/fstab or mounting asks for administrator rights through polkit
(pkexec), or uses sudo if it is configured without a password.
.PP
Only one window runs at a time; starting the app again brings the existing window forward.
.PP
A splash screen is shown at startup and closes after 15 seconds; the ? button in the bottom\-left
corner shows the same information (About) until closed.
.SH AUTHOR
csTechnologies, https://cstevens.ca
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WIDTHxHEIGHT"
Initial window size (default 1240x820).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Do not send a desktop notification (via notify\-send) when a disk is plugged in.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FSTABCTL_FSTAB, FSTABCTL_BACKUP_DIR, FSTABCTL_HOME
As for
.BR fstabctl (1).
.TP
.B DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY
pkexec is used only when one of these is set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/fstabctl/backups/
Shared with
.BR fstabctl (1).
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit\-1/actions/org.fstabctl.manager.policy
Polkit action describing the password prompt.
.SH NOTES
Run it as your normal user and let polkit ask for your password when needed. The command
.B fstabctl\-gui
is kept as a link to this program for compatibility.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fstabctl (1)
.PP
Full documentation: /usr/share/doc/fstab-manager/
